'''Pau'ans''' were gaunt, long-limbed [[humanoid]]s from [[Utapau]]. They dwelled in their [[planet]]'s sinkholes, and tamed the local [[varactyl]] for riding. Due to their long life-span, they were also known as '''the Ancients'''. The [[Utai]], another indigenous [[species]] that lived on Utapau, along with the Pau'ans, were collectively known as the '''[[Utapaun]]s'''.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Pauan_Jedi_Teacher_DoH.png|thumb|left|180px|A female Pau'an]]
The Pau'ans were a [[species]] of gaunt [[humanoid]]s with [[Color|gray]], furrowed skin, and sunken [[eye]]s. Their [[Limb|arms]] ended in long, pentadactyl hands with an opposable thumb and sharp nails.<ref name="ROS" /> Being [[Diet|carnivores]] with a preference for raw meat,<ref name="VG" /> they also had sharp, jagged [[Tooth|teeth]].<ref name="DBpau" /> In addition to those intimidating features, Pau'ans were tall&mdash;[[Tion Medon]], a [[Port Administrator]] during the [[Clone Wars]], stood at about 2.06 [[meter]]s.<ref name="DBtio">{{Databank|tion-medon|Tion Medon}}</ref> Pau'ans had two stomachs.<ref name="Last Shot">''[[Last Shot]]''</ref> They had hypersensitive hearing, which prompted them to wear special coverings to protect their fragile [[ear]]s. Their life-span was measured in centuries, which earned them the nickname of "Ancients".<ref name="AEYNTK" /> They had red blood.

==Society and culture==
The Pau'ans were [[Sentience|sentient]] beings, capable of intelligent thought.<ref name="ROS" /> Although they often appeared fearsome to outsiders, most of them were peaceful and amiable.<ref name="AotG" /> On their [[homeworld]] of [[Utapau]], they preferred to dwell in darkness rather than light,<ref name="VG" /> and their [[City|cities]] were built within the [[planet]]'s many sinkholes.<ref name="DButa">{{Databank|utapau|Utapau}}</ref>

<div style="float:right">[[File:PauanEarCovering-SWBC68.png|thumb|left|180px|Pau'ans wore special covers to protect their ears.]]</div>
Pau'ans shared Utapau with at least three other species, namely the [[Utai]], the [[Sugi]], and the [[Amani]].<ref name="DoU" /> The Utai were a fellow indigenous species on Utapau, with whom the Pau'ans had a symbiotic relationship. The two races were collectively referred to as Utapauns.<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> Like the Utai, the Pau'ans built their cities and buildings in the [[Ossic architecture|Ossic architectural]] form.<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> The primary Pau'an settlement and [[spaceport]] on Utapau was [[Pau City]], which was administrated by various officials including the [[Governor]], the Police Inspector,<ref name="DoU">{{TCW|A Death on Utapau}}</ref> and the Port Administrator.<ref name="ROS" />

The Pau'ans' native [[language]] was [[Utapese]],<ref name="AEYNTK" /> but they were also capable of speaking [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="ROS" /> Some Pau'an's, such as [[Gen Tri]] of the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]], used the [[gender]]-neutral singular pronoun "they, them".<ref name="Free Fall">''[[Poe Dameron: Free Fall]]''</ref>

It was typical for creatures to be freshly slain every day for meals on Utapau, rather than being killed and then cooked or stored for later consumption, due to the Pau'an preference for raw meat.<ref name="AEYNTK" /> They domesticated the fast-paced [[varactyl]] to use as mounts.<ref name="DBvar">{{Databank|varactyl|Varactyl}}</ref>

==History==
===Development and Republic Era===
[[File:Pauan_and_Utai_DoH.png|thumb|left|200px|A Pau'an ambassador confers with two Utai.]]
Originally, the Pau'ans occupied the surface of Utapau, while the Utai lived in tunnels and caverns. Over time, however, [[hyperwind storm]]s became more frequent all across the planet and forced the Pau'ans underground. The two societies then merged and started founding sinkhole cities.<ref name="AEYNTK" />

At the end of the [[Clone Wars]], the planet was [[Invasion of Utapau|occupied]] by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. The [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] came searching for [[General]] [[Grievous]]: Port Administrator Tion Medon discreetly informed him of Grievous's location, allowing him to bring the [[Grand Army of the Republic|forces of the Republic]] to [[Battle of Utapau|liberate]] the Pau'ans.<ref name="ROS" />

During the Clone Wars, a [[The Grand Inquisitor|Pau'an male]] served the [[Jedi Order]] as a [[Jedi Temple Guard]].<ref name="Shroud of Darkness" /> The same Pau'an would turn to the [[dark side of the Force]] and attain the title of [[Grand Inquisitor]], the leader of the [[Galactic Empire|Empire's]] [[Inquisitorius]].<ref name="VG" />

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Do you think I wanted Utapau to join the Empire? The compromises I made created a future for my people."<br />"I've been to Utapau, Senator. They spit your name out like a curse."<br />"Out least they are alive!|[[Bode Akuna]] joins Imperial Senator Daho Sejan and [[Cal Kestis]]' conversation|<ref name="Star Wars Jedi: Survivor" />}}
[[File:SW42-AlanQuah-GrandInquisitor-ImperialCog.png|thumb|right|200px|The Grand Inquisitor was a Pau'an]]
During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the Empire, many Pau'ans fled their homeworld after it was [[Occupation of Utapau|occupied by the Empire]].<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> Although Imperial [[Senator]] Pau'an [[Daho Sejan]] was against the idea of Utapau joining the Galactic Empire, he made concessions, which in his words, gave his people a future. However, most Pau'ans did not agree with Sejan, so much so that they would spit in contempt when they heard the senator's name.<ref name="Star Wars Jedi: Survivor">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]''</ref>

At the time of the [[Battle of Yavin]], a [[Unidentified Pau'an drug dealer|Pau'an drug dealer]] worked at a [[Unidentified cantina (Level 1997)|cantina]] on [[Coruscant]]. He would recruit strays to make deliveries. [[Anandra Milon]] visited him with [[Santigo Milon|her brother]] to find shelter, but refused and fled when a [[stormtrooper]] and [[Coruscant underworld police|underworld policeman]] arrived.<ref name="OTLD">{{InsiderCite|151|One Thousand Levels Down}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Grand_Inquisitor_on_Daiyu.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The Pau'an design featured in ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'']]
The design of the Pau'ans for [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']] was originally intended for the [[Mustafarian|natives]] of [[Mustafar]].<ref name="Tbone">{{WebCite|url=http://starwarz.com/tbone/unused-concepts|text=Unused Concepts|work=[https://starwarz.com/tbone T-bone's Star Wars Universe]|archivedate=20201224013332}}</ref> The Pau'ans themselves were designed as [[Wikipedia:lemur|lemur]]-like creatures per [[George Lucas]].<ref name="Databank">{{DB|species|utapaun|Utapaun}}</ref> These lemur concepts would later become the [[Lurmen]].<ref name="DB-Lurmen">{{DB|species|lurmen|Lurmen}}</ref> Artist [[Sang Jun Lee]] drew some initial sketches of the Pau'an species, and [[Robert E. Barnes]] and [[Michael Murnane]] created sculptures of their faces. The design developed over time and was later changed to the Pau'ans' current appearance as ''Revenge of the Sith'' developed.<ref name="Aliens">{{InsiderCite|90|Aliens of Episode III}}</ref> The Pau'ans in ''Revenge of the Sith'' were created through a mix of prosthetic makeup effects and [[Wiki:Computer-generated imagery|computer-generated imagery]].<ref name="Databank" /> The design of their face was inspired by an African tribal mask.<ref name="Star Wars.com article">{{SWArchive|url=episode-iii/bts/profile/f20050623/index.html|text=Alien Sophistication: Bruce Spence as Tion Medon}}</ref> For the [[Disney+]] streaming series ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'', the Grand Inquisitor, and by extension the Pau'an species, was redesigned<ref name="Part I">{{Kenobi|Part I}}</ref> despite its prior appearance in a live action production via ''Revenge of the Sith''.<ref name="ROS" />

